# The Flow field view of a REAL 3D solve, not the demo: the example rocket's drag table and its 3D angles (2 and 6 degrees at the
# Mach nodes) are solved on the GPU as the app solves them, in one solve that choosing the method starts; the headless driver waits for every
# running task, so each click returns when the solve is done (a few minutes in all). The picture is the final Field3 of the stability solve at one Mach number: the finned example on the 3D grid.
# GPU pictures need the wgpu test backend, a real solve the GPU: through the queue,
#   tools/gpuq/gpuq submit --host local --name flow3d-real -- env ICED_TEST_BACKEND=wgpu cargo run --release -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/flow3d-real.drive out/flow3d-real
viewport 1500x1100
click "Analyze"
click "CFD table"
click "Flow field"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot field-default-dark.png

# the angle stepper: the drag solve's meridian at 0 degrees, then the 3D solve's 2 and 6 degrees
click "▶"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot field-2deg-dark.png
click "Schlieren"
click "Side"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot field-2deg-plane-schlieren-dark.png
click "3/4"
click "▶"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot field-6deg-schlieren-dark.png
click "Mach"
click "Cross-flow"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot field-6deg-cross-dark.png
move (900, 560)
move (902, 562)
screenshot field-6deg-hover-dark.png
